### What pa3ds calls Omega Ruby and Alpha Sapphire's pictures that the game never names, by the
### name of the picture's texture less `.bclim`. Said whole in place of the texture's own words,
### and ahead of the words every game shares (`data/common/en/pictures.ftl`).

# The opening's choice of boy or girl: a portrait each on the handheld's screen, `intro_male` and
# `intro_famale` (findings, spike 71). Read off the replays' pictures, enlarged
# (OR_character-desc.ctm as the boy, 2026-10-15, and OR_character-desc2.ctm as the girl,
# 2026-10-16); each one's clothes from the screen turning them round once chosen.
texture-intro_male = Boy, fair skin, brown hair, grey-blue eyes, a wide toothy grin, black knit hat with a white top and an orange emblem on the front, red short-sleeved shirt with black panels, green backpack, black trousers
texture-intro_famale = Girl, fair skin with rosy cheeks, light-brown shoulder-length hair that flicks out at the ends, grey-blue eyes, an open smile, a red bandana with white stripes tied in a big bow on top of her head, red sleeveless top with a black collar, green-and-yellow pouch at her hip

# Words the intro and the title screen draw as pictures, as a sighted player reads them: the
# intro's credit over the pond, `presented_by` and `gf_logo`, and the title screen's blinking
# prompt, `push_start` (spike 236). Said in their descriptions (`{ PICTURE("push_start") }`).
texture-presented_by = Presented by
texture-gf_logo = Game Freak
texture-push_start = Press Start
